    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8c88bcb_ebdd3b7d",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1514,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288462
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-23T10:06:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It only when we are in PD_STATE_SRC_READY state will have this if case. And first time only having power contract before can transit to PD_STATE_SRC_READY state. Once having power contract  caps_count and hard_reset_count variables must be reset when leaving PD_STATE_SRC_DISCOVERY state. Other cases(ex.PD_STATE_SRC_GET_SNK_CAP or requested power data from SNK can\u0027t match SRC_CAP)which transit to PD_STATE_SRC_READY state won\u0027t increase caps_count. So if SRC port  receives PD_CTRL_GET_SOURCE_CAP control message in PD_STATE_SRC_READY state, the caps_count is still zero. I think there is not the case that you\u0027re concerned.\n\nOk, thanks that.",
      "parentUuid": "8433313f_eba9422b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1514,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 1514,
        "endChar": 43
      },
